@@ -5,6 +5,30 @@ description: Orchestrator reference for pi-messenger Crew planning, task managem
 
 # Pi-Messenger Crew Skill
 
+## Vertrice staged integration (takes precedence over upstream examples below)
+
+This is the full Messenger/Crew package, not a transport-only adapter. Initial
+execution uses strict dependencies, one worker (max one), minimal coordination,
+and the current native Node/Pi runtime and selected session model. No new provider
+or agent-frontmatter fallback model is selected by this integration.
+
+Use `plan` with `autoWork: false`, inspect `task.list` / `crew.validate`, then use
+explicit `work` with `concurrency: 1`. Plan/review/work remain real Crew actions.
+The overlay does not start/refill workers from rendering or capacity keys;
+explicit task start is still an execution action. Auto-overlay defaults are off.
+
+Keep one coordinator per Crew cwd and no overlapping plan/work/revise/manual
+mutation during a worker run. This is a conservative operating envelope, not a
+fix for upstream's multi-writer task/plan/spec races. Sequential public tool calls
+and one worker do not serialize other sessions, direct store writers or overlays.
+Do not wipe/replan a durable backlog. Migration and retirement of old task tooling
+are a separate cutover; do not maintain two writable mirrors.
+
+Worker scope, privilege/sign-in handoffs and owner acceptance stay explicit.
+`task.done`, reviewer SHIP, and plan completion do not establish owner acceptance.
+A send publication is not recipient ACK; failed inbox files are retained and may
+replay. Do not run upstream `install.mjs` or contents-blind legacy uninstall.
+
 > Crew workers do not need this skill. `crew-worker.md` already contains every `pi_messenger` action workers need for task execution.
 >
 > Orchestrators and humans can use this as the full reference for planning, task management, configuration, and Crew internals.
